We need to output the corrected HTML file. The only change requested: add controls to the start screen as their own short lines. The test report says everything else works, keep everything else exactly as it is. So we need to modify showStartScreen to include controls lines. The overlay has elements: title, msg, final, best, prompt. We can set msg to goal, and add controls perhaps in prompt? But prompt currently says "Press any key or click to start". The brief says start screen with title, one-line goal and controls; any key or click starts. The test report says start screen shows title, goal and best score but NOT controls. Add controls as their own short lines, for example:
"← → or A / D: move   ·   Space / ↓ / S: lower, grab, drop"
"Tap Space twice quickly = fast drop (breaks eggs!)   ·   R: restart"
Change only the start screen text; keep everything else exactly as it is.

We need to add controls lines. The overlay has p elements: msg, final, best, prompt. We can set msg to goal, and maybe add a new <p> for controls? But "Change only the start screen text" means we can modify the HTML structure? The instruction says "Change only the start screen text; keep everything else exactly as it is." That likely means we can add a new <p> element for controls in the overlay, or we can put controls into existing elements. The example shows two lines. We could set msg to goal, and then add a new <p id="controls"> with the two lines. But that would be changing the HTML structure, not just text. However, the instruction says "Change only the start screen text" meaning we should only modify the text content of the start screen, not other parts. Adding a new element is arguably changing the start screen markup, but it's still part of the start screen. The safest is to use existing elements: we have msg, final, best, prompt. We could set msg to the goal, and then set prompt to include controls and start hint? But prompt is used for "Press R to play again" on win/lose. On start screen, prompt is "Press any key or click to start". We could change prompt to include controls and start hint, but that would be a single line. The example shows two lines. We could set msg to goal, and then add a new <p> for controls. But the instruction says "Change only the start screen text" - I think adding a new <p> is acceptable because it's part of the start screen. However, to be safe, we can modify the existing elements: set msg to goal, and then set prompt to the controls lines plus start hint? But prompt is a single <p>, we can put line breaks with <br>. The example shows two lines. We can set prompt.textContent to "← → or A / D: move   ·   Space / ↓ / S: lower, grab, drop\nTap Space twice quickly = fast drop (breaks eggs!)   ·   R: restart\nPress any key or click to start" but that would be three lines. The brief says "any key or click starts" and the test report says start screen shows title, goal and best score but NOT controls. So we need to add controls. The example shows two lines. We can put them in a new <p> or we can put them in msg? But msg is the goal. Let's look at the current showStartScreen:

function showStartScreen() {
    title.textContent = 'Gripper Rush';
    msg.textContent = 'Sort 20 objects into the correct bins before you run out of 3 lives.';
    final.textContent = '';
    best.textContent = 'Best score: ' + bestScore;
    prompt.textContent = 'Press any key or click to start';
    overlay.classList.add('show');
}

We can change msg to include goal and controls? But the goal is one line. The example shows controls as separate lines. We could set msg to the goal, and then add a new <p id="controls"> in the HTML. But the instruction says "Change only the start screen text" - I think adding a new element is fine because it's part of the start screen. However, to be minimal, we can modify the existing prompt to include controls and start hint. But the example shows two lines for controls, and then "Press any key or click to start" is separate. We could set prompt to "Press any key or click to start" and add a new <p> for controls. Let's see the overlay HTML:

<div id="overlay">
    <h1 id="title">Gripper Rush</h1>
    <p id="msg"></p>
    <p id="final"></p>
    <p id="best"></p>
    <p id="prompt"></p>
</div>

We can add a <p id="controls"></p> after msg. Then in showStartScreen, set controls.textContent to the two lines. That would be a change to the HTML structure, but it's still the start screen. The instruction says "Change only the start screen text" - I think it's acceptable. Alternatively, we can put the controls into msg by using <br> but msg is the goal. The goal is one line. We could set msg to the goal, and then set prompt to the controls and start hint. But prompt is used for "Press R to play again" on win/lose. On start screen, we can set prompt to the controls and start hint. But the example shows two lines for controls, and then "Press any key or click to start" is separate. We could set prompt to "Press any key or click to start" and add a new <p> for controls. I think adding a new <p> is the cleanest.

